+- `docs/harness-toml.md`: both rows, and the table's intro says what `off` means and that redaction still applies with `secret_print` down.
+- `errors.md`: an L011 row in the E120 table, and a short note on L014 after it. `troubleshooting.md`: L011 and L014 rows, and "printing an env var's value" in the hard-rule row. Both READMEs' guardrails name it.
+- §3.1's tables and §5's hard-rule keys list both rules.
+- `skills/notebook/SKILL.md`, under "Never": show a secret or any piece of it (prefix, length, masked preview); check a key with `print("OPENAI_API_KEY" in os.environ)`; nh refuses showing its value (L011). The advice is stricter than L011, which lets `len` through. Two two-line bullets elsewhere became one line each, so the file stays at 150 lines. Round 1 of the eval below is why it is there.
